This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

Its subject is scripts/validate-shell-portability.sh, which is this repository's own
pre-push validator. install.sh does not ship it, so on a consumer this fixture would
resolve no validator at all and could only pass.

It is also a MUTATION BATTERY: it builds one throwaway git repo per unit, each carrying a
copy of the validator and a seeded shell file, and asserts one arm fires per repo. The unit
count is derived and printed by the run itself; it is not quoted here, because every raw
total written into this tree has gone stale while reading exactly like a fresh one.
